> Receiver contract (K17, word for word): `books[].audio.wordClips` (object: lower-case word ->
> relative file path) and `song.videoLeadInSeconds` (number, seconds). The key is the K2 form of
> the tapped word: NFC, U+2019 and U+2018 to U+0027, lower case, outer characters other than a to
> z and the apostrophe removed, and the key must match `^[a-z]+('[a-z]+)*$`. The value is relative
> to `content/storytime/`, as `books[].audio.file` is. A word with no key has no clip and no tap
> target. Listen points of the 27 new clips (K10): w02 `wa-how.mp3` (text "How"), `wa-oh.mp3`
> (text "Oh"), `wa-suns.mp3` (note "heard 'sons' in 3 takes"); w03 `wa-it.mp3` (text "It"); w04
> `wa-this.mp3` (text "This"); w06 `wa-he.mp3` (text "He"); w07 `wa-run.mp3` (text "Run"),
